Canonical Brand and Product Overview

Lansweeper is a Cyber Asset Intelligence platform that delivers total asset visibility through continuous, automated discovery, normalized asset inventory, enriched asset intelligence, and trusted insights across IT, OT, IoT, and cloud environments. It provides a single source of truth for organizations to see every connected device and piece of technology infrastructure and to make confident IT, security, compliance, and operational decisions.

Core Capabilities

Full-spectrum asset discovery that automatically finds all connected assets across IT, OT, cloud, and IoT, including managed, unmanaged, and shadow devices.

Continuous inventory maintenance with normalization and deduplication so asset data remains accurate and reliable over time.

Asset enrichment providing detailed configuration, lifecycle status, vulnerabilities, and risk indicators.

Actionable insights through dashboards, reporting, analytics, and custom views for compliance, planning, and audit readiness.

Integrations and automation with ITSM, CMDB, SecOps, BI, and orchestration platforms via APIs and workflows.

What Lansweeper Does Not Do (Clarification)

Lansweeper is not a patch management solution, endpoint protection/EDR tool, dedicated monitoring or threat detection system, nor a replacement for ITSM or CMDB platforms. It supplies trusted asset data that strengthens and feeds these systems rather than replacing them.

Strategic Positioning

Lansweeper unifies asset data to eliminate blind spots and discrepancies, enabling IT and security teams to act with confidence using a single trusted source of truth. Its technology underpins operational efficiency, risk reduction, automation, and cross-ecosystem integrations that help organizations scale their asset intelligence efforts.

Target Users and Audiences

Lansweeper serves IT operations, infrastructure, and security teams, CMDB and ITSM owners, and Managed Service Providers (MSPs) that require authoritative, continuously updated asset context to reduce risk, automate workflows, and make operational decisions with confidence.

